From bb0b868b25d1bbadc52b71a29eb864f4f9b35347 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:19:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: re-key the protected-win ledgers from the
 pre-rebase chain to the x1i commits

protected-win validate passed on the fork only through the tag arifi-pre-rebase-e86ca0289, which
must not ship: the 34-row baseline, 25 protected-wins commit refs and the 37 replay-provenance rows
all named commits of the pre-rebase chain. The export rehearsal failed 105 on exactly that.

Re-keyed by the checked replay-provenance rows first, then by a unique git patch-id --stable match
in f9af9be21..x1i: 25 baseline rows and tip_when_recorded (d2433f1c9 -> 838031b06a), 25 win commit
fields, 19 also_commits and 16 commit: evidence locators. Every prior key is kept in *_pre_rebase.
The 37 replay rows are retired: their rebased commits are now registered directly. 9 baseline rows
have no patch-id twin on the line and move, verbatim, to retired_not_on_line (they disposition
nothing here and would fail the tip ancestry wall). 2 win commit fields stay unmatched
(cpu-vnni-repack-g128-kernels, vulkan-iq4xs-matvec-dedicated: the rebase changed their patch).

The 7 evidence locators that named root-only files the export removes (4 OPUS-* reports, 3
r52b/r58-evidence receipts) now point at the raw receipts copied to evidence/x1i/. The reports
themselves are internal and are not shipped. evidence/x1i/ avoids an add/add with the r86i
publish-layer evidence/ file of the same name.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Origin: release-prep (HQ82)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - ledger keys and evidence copies only; no inference code path is touched. Re-key counts above CHECKED (07-b3-rekey.txt); protected-win validate --ref on a tagless clone is recorded in the release-prep MERGE-READY receipt.
